// Inside the box (IN-MIRROR, MAGIC-MIRROR). Its ways out depend on which
// of its two doors is open and which way the box has been turned, and
// lead to a place that is not written anywhere a direction could name, so
// each leads to the landing, which carries whoever arrives on to where
// the box's state says (adventurer.sprout's `:mirror_out`).
kind MirrorBox is sprout.Place {
  grammar { article none }
  passage closed_box { You are inside a closed box! }
  passage wall_there { There's a wall there. }
  passage hit_panels { You would hit one of the panels.{if underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)} The pine door stands open to the {self.pine_dir}, and that is the way out through it.{/if}{if underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open)} The mirror stands open to the {self.mirror_dir}, and that is the way out through it.{/if} }
  describe { text full }
  passage full {
    Inside Mirror

    You are inside a rectangular box of wood whose structure is rather complicated. Four sides and the roof are filled in, and the floor is open.

    As you face the side opposite the entrance, two short sides of carved and polished wood are to your left and right. The left panel is mahogany, the right pine. The wall you face is red on its left half and black on its right. On the entrance side, the wall is white opposite the red part of the wall it faces, and yellow opposite the black section. The painted walls are at least twice the length of the unpainted ones. The ceiling is painted blue.

    In the floor is a stone channel about six inches wide and a foot deep. The channel is oriented in a north-south direction. In the exact center of the room the channel widens into a circular depression perhaps two feet wide. Incised in the stone around this area is a compass rose.

    Running from one short wall to the other at about waist height is a wooden bar, carefully carved and drilled. This bar is pierced in two places. The first hole is in the center of the bar (and thus the center of the room). The second is at the left end of the room (as you face opposite the entrance). Through each hole runs a wooden pole.

    The pole at the left end of the bar is short, extending about a foot above the bar, and ends in a hand grip. The pole {if underground_caverns_3.get(:mloc) == 2 && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 270}{if underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) != 0}has been lifted out of a hole carved in the stone floor. There is evidently enough friction to keep the pole from dropping back down.{else}has been dropped into a hole carved in the stone floor.{/if}{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 0 || underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 180}{if underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) != 0}is positioned above the stone channel in the floor.{else}has been dropped into the stone channel incised in the floor.{/if}{else}is resting on the stone floor.{/if}

    The long pole at the center of the bar extends from the ceiling through the bar to the circular area in the stone channel. This bottom end of the pole has a T-bar a bit less than two feet long attached to it, and on the T-bar is carved an arrow. The arrow and T-bar are pointing {self.arrow}.{if underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)}

    The pine panel has been opened outward, to the {self.pine_dir}; the hallway shows through it, and sees in through it.{/if}{if underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open)}

    The mirror on the entrance side stands open, and the hallway shows through it.{/if}

    {self.objects}
  }
  // The pine door is the short wall opposite the arrow, and the mirror
  // the long wall on the entrance side, a quarter-turn widdershins of it.
  passage pine_dir { {if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 0}south{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 45}southwest{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 90}west{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 135}northwest{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 180}north{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 225}northeast{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 270}east{else}southeast{/if} }
  passage mirror_dir { {if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 0}west{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 45}northwest{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 90}north{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 135}northeast{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 180}east{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 225}southeast{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 270}south{else}southwest{/if} }
  passage arrow { {if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 0}north{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 45}northeast{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 90}east{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 135}southeast{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 180}south{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 225}southwest{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 270}west{else}northwest{/if} }
  passage objects {
    {for t: Thing in self}{if !t.get(:ndesc)}

    {t.ldesc}{/if}{/for}
  }
  as target for any { permit { refuse "You can't see any such thing." } }
  as tool for any { permit { refuse "You can't see any such thing." } }
  on :mirror_shut { tell "The mirror quietly swings shut." }
  on :wood_shut { tell "The pine wall closes quietly." }
}

object in_mirror is MirrorBox in underground_caverns_3 {
  grammar {
    name "Inside Mirror"
    exit out "out" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) || underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit out "out" refuse closed_box
    exit north "north" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 90)
    exit north "north" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit north "north" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 180)
    exit north "north" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit north "north" refuse closed_box
    exit northeast "northeast" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 135)
    exit northeast "northeast" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit northeast "northeast" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit northeast "northeast" refuse closed_box
    exit east "east" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 180)
    exit east "east" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit east "east" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit east "east" refuse closed_box
    exit southeast "southeast" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 225)
    exit southeast "southeast" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit southeast "southeast" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit southeast "southeast" refuse closed_box
    exit south "south" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 270)
    exit south "south" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit south "south" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 0)
    exit south "south" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit south "south" refuse closed_box
    exit southwest "southwest" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 315)
    exit southwest "southwest" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit southwest "southwest" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit southwest "southwest" refuse closed_box
    exit west "west" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 0)
    exit west "west" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit west "west" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit west "west" refuse closed_box
    exit northwest "northwest" -> mirror_landing when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir) == 45)
    exit northwest "northwest" refuse wall_there when (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open))
    exit northwest "northwest" refuse hit_panels when (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open))
    exit northwest "northwest" refuse closed_box
    exit up "up" refuse "The roof is filled in, and painted blue, and no nearer for being looked at."
    exit down "down" refuse "The floor of the box is open, and under it is the stone floor of the hallway, which you are standing on already."
  }
  object floor is Floor
  object ceiling is Scenery {
    grammar { name "ceiling"  nouns "roof"  adjectives "blue", "painted" }
    passage short { ceiling }
    describe { text "The roof of the box, painted blue, a flat and confident blue such as the sky is said to be. The long pole goes up into it." }
  }
  object red_panel is BoxPanel { :which red  grammar { name "red panel"  nouns "panel", "wall", "half", "side"  adjectives "red", "left" }  passage short { red panel } }
  object black_panel is BoxPanel { :which black  grammar { name "black panel"  nouns "panel", "wall", "half", "side"  adjectives "black", "right" }  passage short { black panel } }
  object white_panel is BoxPanel { :which white  grammar { name "white panel"  nouns "panel", "wall", "half", "side"  adjectives "white", "entrance" }  passage short { white panel } }
  object yellow_panel is BoxPanel { :which yellow  grammar { name "yellow panel"  nouns "panel", "wall", "half", "side"  adjectives "yellow" }  passage short { yellow panel } }
  object mahogany_panel is BoxPanel { :which mahogany  grammar { name "mahogany panel"  nouns "panel", "wall", "side", "mahogany"  adjectives "mahogany", "left", "short" }  passage short { mahogany panel } }
  object pine_panel is BoxPanel { :which pine  grammar { name "pine panel"  nouns "panel", "wall", "door", "side", "pine"  adjectives "pine", "right", "short" }  passage short { pine panel } }
  object t_bar is Scenery, Touchable {
    grammar { name "T-bar"  nouns "t-bar", "bar", "tbar", "crossbar"  adjectives "carved", "short" }
    passage short { T-bar }
    describe { text "A bar a little under two feet long, fixed across the bottom end of the long pole where it meets the floor, and carved with an arrow. The arrow is pointing {if here.is(MirrorBox)}{here.arrow}{else}somewhere{/if}. It is the box's way of saying which way it faces, and it is the only part of the box that does not move when you push it." }
    as target for turn { do { say "You don't have enough leverage to turn the T-bar. You might be able to turn the whole structure, however." } }
    as target for shift { do { say "You don't have enough leverage to turn the T-bar. You might be able to turn the whole structure, however." } }
    as target for rub { do { say "Smooth old wood, and the arrow's groove under your thumb." } }
    passage no_take { It is fixed to the pole, and the pole to the box, and the box to its own idea of itself. }
  }
  object long_pole is Scenery, Touchable {
    grammar { name "long pole"  nouns "pole", "pivot"  adjectives "long", "center", "central", "wooden" }
    passage short { long pole }
    describe { text "A wooden pole as thick as your wrist, running from the ceiling through the center of the bar to the circular depression in the channel below, where it ends in the T-bar. Everything else in the box is arranged round it; it is the pivot the box turns on, and it does not turn itself." }
    // Refused from a `permit`, so that a bare "pole" raised, lowered or
    // pushed is the short one, whose consent allows (the spec's Choosing
    // a reading); named "long", it answers in these words.
    as target for raise { permit { refuse "The long pole goes through the roof and into the floor, and is not a thing a person lifts." } }
    as target for lower { permit { refuse "It is as low as a pole can be that goes through the floor already." } }
    as target for shift { permit { refuse "The pole does not move; the box moves round it, if the box moves." } }
    as target for turn { permit { refuse "You don't have enough leverage. You might be able to turn the whole structure, however." } }
    as target for rub { do { say "Old wood, polished by hands, most of them, you suspect, in a hurry." } }
    passage no_take { It goes through the roof and into the floor. }
  }
  object short_pole is ShortPole
  object wooden_bar is Scenery, Touchable {
    grammar { name "wooden bar"  nouns "bar", "crossbar"  adjectives "wooden", "wood", "carved", "drilled" }
    passage short { wooden bar }
    describe { text "A bar of wood running from one short wall to the other at about the height of your waist, carefully carved and drilled: two holes through it, one at the center of the room for the long pole and one at the left end for the short. It is what you would hold on to, if the box did anything sudden." }
    as target for rub { do { say "Solid, and very slightly sticky, as old varnish is." } }
    as target for turn { do { say "The bar is fixed at both ends." } }
    passage no_take { It is fixed to the walls at both ends. }
  }
  object compass_arrow is Scenery {
    grammar { name "compass arrow"  nouns "arrow", "indicator"  adjectives "compass", "carved" }
    passage short { compass arrow }
    describe { text "The arrow carved on the T-bar, pointing {if here.is(MirrorBox)}{here.arrow}{else}somewhere{/if}. Below it, round the depression in the channel, the compass rose it points at." }
    passage no_take { It is carved into the T-bar. }
  }
  object rose is Rose
  object channel is Channel
  object guardians is Guardians
}

// The landing: never read, only passed through (MIROUT).
object mirror_landing is sprout.Place in underground_caverns_3 {
  grammar { name "Inside Mirror"  article none }
  describe { text "You are between the box and the hallway, and then you are not." }
  on :entered (item, from) {
    if (item.is(Adventurer)) { send item :mirror_out }
  }
}

// A panel of the box's inside (MPANELS, MENDS): the red and yellow ones
// turn the box clockwise when pushed, the black and white ones
// counterclockwise, once the short pole is up; the mahogany one slides
// the box along the channel, the way the arrow points, when the box
// stands along it; the pine one swings open, into the hallway, for five
// moves.
kind BoxPanel is Scenery, Touchable, Openable {
  :which Panel default red
  :dying false
  describe {
    if (self.get(:which) == :mahogany) { text "A short wall of mahogany, dark and close-grained and polished to a glow, to your left as you face away from the entrance. It is the wall the arrow points at, and from the look of the wear on it, the one that gets pushed." }
    else if (self.get(:which) == :pine) { text pine_looked_at }
    else if (self.get(:which) == :red) { text "The left half of the wall you face, painted red, a long wall; the paint is old and the red has gone the colour of brick. Pushing on it, you would think, would push the box round." }
    else if (self.get(:which) == :black) { text "The right half of the wall you face, painted black, a long wall; the black has stayed black, as black does. Pushing on it, you would think, would push the box round the other way." }
    else if (self.get(:which) == :white) { text "The white half of the entrance wall, opposite the red; it is the wall the mirror is mounted on, from the other side, and white so that you could tell it from the yellow." }
    else { text "The yellow half of the entrance wall, opposite the black; the mirror is on the far side of it, and the yellow is to tell it from the white, which is all a colour is for in here." }
  }
  passage pine_looked_at { A short wall of pine, pale against the mahogany opposite, to your right as you face away from the entrance{if here.is(MirrorBox)}, which is to say on the {here.pine_dir} side of the box as it stands now{/if}. {if underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)}It stands open outward, on hinges along one edge, and the hallway shows through it; which is to say that the hallway sees in through it, and anything that watches the hallway sees whatever the box is carrying.{else}There is a line down one edge of it that might be a hinge, and no handle. It is the box's door, and a door the hallway would show through is a door the hallway could see through.{/if} }
  as target for close { do { say "You can't do that to the panel." } }
  as target for open {
    do {
      if (self.get(:which) == :pine) { self.set(:pushed, true) }
      else { say "You don't see a way to open the panel here; it is a wall of the box, and the box has the two doors it has." }
      if (self.get(:pushed)) {
        self.set(:pushed, false)
        let md = underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir)
        let ml = underground_caverns_3.get(:mloc)
        if (md != 0 && md != 180) { say "The structure rocks back and forth slightly but doesn't move." }
        else if (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)) { say "The pine wall is open already." }
        else {
          say "The pine wall swings open."
          if ((ml == 5 && md == 0) || (ml == 3 && md == 180) || ml == 4) {
            if (underground_caverns_3.get(:guardians_seen)) { say "The pine door opens into the field of view of the Guardians." }
            else { say "The pine door opens into the field of view of the Guardians of Zork, represented by two identical stone statues carrying bludgeons." }
            say "The Guardians awake, and in perfect unison, utterly destroy you with their stone bludgeons. Satisfied, they resume their posts."
            if (actor.is(Adventurer)) { send actor :die }
          }
          else {
            send underground_caverns_3 :wood_set with true
            say "{if here.is(MirrorBox)}It opens to the {here.pine_dir}, onto the hallway, which shows through the doorway and would see in through it as readily: while it stands open, whatever is in the box is in plain view of whatever is in the hall.{else}It opens onto the hallway, which shows through the doorway and would see in through it as readily.{/if}"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  :pushed false
  as target for shift {
    do {
      let md = underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir)
      let ml = underground_caverns_3.get(:mloc)
      // The door (MENDS, I-PININ): the pine wall swings open into the
      // hallway, unless the hallway it swings into is the Guardians'.
      if (self.get(:which) == :pine) {
        if (md != 0 && md != 180) { say "The structure rocks back and forth slightly but doesn't move." }
        else if (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)) { say "The pine wall is open already." }
        else {
          say "The pine wall swings open."
          if ((ml == 5 && md == 0) || (ml == 3 && md == 180) || ml == 4) {
            if (underground_caverns_3.get(:guardians_seen)) { say "The pine door opens into the field of view of the Guardians." }
            else { say "The pine door opens into the field of view of the Guardians of Zork, represented by two identical stone statues carrying bludgeons." }
            say "The Guardians awake, and in perfect unison, utterly destroy you with their stone bludgeons. Satisfied, they resume their posts."
            if (actor.is(Adventurer)) { send actor :die }
          }
          else {
            send underground_caverns_3 :wood_set with true
            say "{if here.is(MirrorBox)}It opens to the {here.pine_dir}, onto the hallway, which shows through the doorway and would see in through it as readily: while it stands open, whatever is in the box is in plain view of whatever is in the hall.{else}It opens onto the hallway, which shows through the doorway and would see in through it as readily.{/if}"
          }
        }
      }
      // The slide (MENDS, MIRMOVE): along the channel, the way the arrow
      // points, one compass rose at a time; into the Guardians' stretch
      // with the pole up, a mirror broken or a door open, a death.
      else if (self.get(:which) == :mahogany) {
        if (md != 0 && md != 180) { say "The structure rocks back and forth slightly but doesn't move." }
        else if (md == 0 && ml == 5) { say "The structure has reached the end of the stone channel and won't budge." }
        else if (md == 180 && ml == 1) { say "The structure has reached the end of the stone channel and won't budge." }
        else {
          self.set(:dying, false)
          if (underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) != 0) { say "The structure sways unsteadily {if md == 0}north{else}south{/if} and stops over another compass rose." }
          else { say "The structure slides {if md == 0}north{else}south{/if} and stops over another compass rose." }
          if (md == 0) { send underground_caverns_3 :mloc_set with ml + 1 } else { send underground_caverns_3 :mloc_set with ml - 1 }
          if ((md == 0 && ml == 3) || (md == 180 && ml == 5)) {
            if (underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) != 0) { self.set(:dying, true) }
            if (!underground_caverns_3.get(:mr1) || !underground_caverns_3.get(:mr2)) { self.set(:dying, true) }
            if (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open) || underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)) { self.set(:dying, true) }
            if (self.get(:dying)) {
              if (underground_caverns_3.get(:guardians_seen)) { say "Suddenly the Guardians realize someone is trying to sneak by them in the structure. They awake and, in perfect unison, hammer the contents of the box (in other words you) to pulp. They then resume their posts, satisfied." }
              else { say "Suddenly, two identical stone bludgeons come through the roof and hammer the contents of the box to pulp. That includes you." }
              if (actor.is(Adventurer)) { send actor :die }
            }
          }
          // A slide made with a door open, short of the Guardians: the
          // open door is heard and felt, so that the next slide is made
          // knowing it (round 8's P1).
          else if (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open) && underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open)) { say "The open pine door swings and creaks on its hinges as the box moves, and the open mirror with it, and the hallway goes by in both gaps; the box is travelling with its two doors open, and anything in the hall that cared to look could look straight in." }
          else if (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)) { say "The open pine door swings and creaks on its hinges as the box moves, and a draught comes through it with the hallway going by in the gap; the box is travelling with its door open, and anything in the hall that cared to look could look straight in." }
          else if (underground_caverns_3.get(:mirror_open)) { say "The open mirror swings a little on its hinge as the box moves, and the hallway goes by in the gap; the box is travelling with its door open, and anything in the hall that cared to look could look straight in." }
        }
      }
      // The turn (MPANELS): clockwise for red and yellow, the other way
      // for black and white, in eighths; in the Guardians' stretch it is
      // a death.
      else if (underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) != 0) {
        if (ml == 4) {
          if (underground_caverns_3.get(:guardians_seen)) { say "The Guardians awake, and in perfect unison, utterly destroy you with their stone bludgeons. Satisfied, they resume their posts." }
          else { say "All at once, two immense stone bludgeons come through the top of the structure, crushing you." }
          if (actor.is(Adventurer)) { send actor :die }
        }
        else {
          if (self.get(:which) == :red || self.get(:which) == :yellow) {
            say "The structure rotates clockwise."
            send underground_caverns_3 :mdir_set with md + 45
            if (md == 315) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates north." }
            else if (md == 0) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates northeast." }
            else if (md == 45) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates east." }
            else if (md == 90) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates southeast." }
            else if (md == 135) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates south." }
            else if (md == 180) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates southwest." }
            else if (md == 225) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates west." }
            else { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates northwest." }
          }
          else {
            say "The structure rotates counterclockwise."
            send underground_caverns_3 :mdir_set with md + 315
            if (md == 45) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates north." }
            else if (md == 90) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates northeast." }
            else if (md == 135) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates east." }
            else if (md == 180) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates southeast." }
            else if (md == 225) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates south." }
            else if (md == 270) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates southwest." }
            else if (md == 315) { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates west." }
            else { say "The arrow on the compass rose now indicates northwest." }
          }
          if (underground_caverns_3.get(:wood_open)) {
            send underground_caverns_3 :wood_set with false
            say "The pine wall closes quietly."
          }
        }
      }
      else if (md == 0 || md == 180) { say "The short pole prevents the structure from rotating." }
      else { say "The structure shakes slightly but doesn't move." }
    }
  }
  as target for rub { do { say "Painted wood, or polished wood; it gives a very little under the hand, and settles back." } }
  as target for mung { do { say "The box was made by somebody who expected it to be kicked, and made it to outlast the kicker." } }
  passage no_take { It is a wall of the box you are standing in. }
}

// The short pole (SHORT-POLE, SHORT-POLE-F): raised, it frees the box to
// turn; dropped into the channel, it steadies the box's slide; dropped
// into the hole at the second rose, it anchors the box where it began.
kind ShortPole is Scenery, Touchable, Placeable {
  grammar { name "short pole"  nouns "pole", "post", "handgrip", "grip"  adjectives "short", "small", "hand" }
  passage short { short pole }
  describe { text "A pole through the left end of the bar, extending about a foot above it and ending in a hand grip, worn smooth. Below the bar it goes down to the floor{if underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) == 0}, and into it{else if underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) == 1}, and rests on it{else}, and stops a little above it, held where it is by friction{/if}. It is the kind of pole that is for pulling up and letting down, and it has been." }
  as target for raise {
    do {
      if (underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup) == 2) { say "The pole cannot be raised further." }
      else {
        send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 2
        say "The pole is now slightly above the floor."
      }
    }
  }
  as target for lower {
    do {
      let p = underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup)
      let md = underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir)
      if (p == 0) { say "The pole cannot be lowered further." }
      else if (md == 0 || md == 180) { send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 0  say "The pole is lowered into the channel." }
      else if (md == 270 && underground_caverns_3.get(:mloc) == 2) { send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 0  say "The pole is lowered into the stone hole." }
      else if (p == 1) { say "The pole is already resting on the floor." }
      else { send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 1  say "The pole now rests on the stone floor." }
    }
  }
  as target for shift {
    do {
      let p = underground_caverns_3.get(:poleup)
      let md = underground_caverns_3.get(:mdir)
      if (p == 0) { say "The pole cannot be lowered further." }
      else if (md == 0 || md == 180) { send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 0  say "The pole is lowered into the channel." }
      else if (md == 270 && underground_caverns_3.get(:mloc) == 2) { send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 0  say "The pole is lowered into the stone hole." }
      else if (p == 1) { say "The pole is already resting on the floor." }
      else { send underground_caverns_3 :pole_set with 1  say "The pole now rests on the stone floor." }
    }
  }
  as target for turn { do { say "The pole turns in your hand, and the box does not turn with it; it is a pin, not a handle." } }
  as target for rub { do { say "The grip is worn to the shape of a hand, and the hand was about the size of yours." } }
  passage no_take { It goes through the bar and would have to come up through it; it comes up a foot, and no more. }
}
